        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 36.171,
        "asr_text": "The disagreement is not really about moving. It is about the source of stability. One worker finds stability in a desk that stays in one place. Papers and a familiar start help this person. The other finds stability in the power to change who is nearby. The kind of space this person needs can also change each day. A shared desk system can even lead people to use the same desk often. So a rule may look flexible on paper but feel difficult to one person. The same system may feel useful to another.",
